;; The single version source. //src:clojars reads it for the pom, the release
;; workflow compares it against the tag, and //bazel/tools:version_consistency
;; keeps the README install snippet in agreement on every bazel test //...
;;
;; 0.1.10, because 0.1.7, 0.1.8 and 0.1.9 are all spent. None exists on Clojars and
;; none can be redeployed ("Non-SNAPSHOT redeploy"), which is why the numbering
;; jumps from 0.1.6:
;;
;;   0.1.7  the publisher uploaded a .sha256; Clojars answers that with 400, after
;;          it had already accepted the jar. Fixed in rules_clj 0.2.1.
;;   0.1.8  every file was accepted with a 201 and the version still never appeared:
;;          Clojars treats the maven-metadata.xml upload as the signal that a deploy
;;          is complete, and the publisher was not sending one. Fixed in rules_clj
;;          0.2.2.
;;   0.1.9  the artifacts uploaded, then the publish refused to finish: reading the
;;          version list got a 302 to Clojars' read mirror and the client would not
;;          follow a redirect. Fixed in rules_clj 0.2.3, which also made --dry-run
;;          perform the reads a real publish performs.
;;
;; Both were found by releasing, and neither could have been found by a dry run.
;;
;; 0.1.5 and not 0.1.0: protoc-gen-clojure's emitter already states runtime
;; floors in generated-code comments — 0.1.3 for the 3-arg rt/message class
;; hint, 0.1.5 for dotted nested-type lookup. The first published artifact
;; satisfies both, so those comments point at a version that really exists.
{:version "0.1.10"}
